                                            PROJECT REPORT – 1
                        Customer Relationship Management System Using Agile Methodology
1. Introduction

The Customer Relationship Management (CRM) System is a software application designed to manage interactions between an organization and its customers effectively. It helps businesses track customer information, manage leads, handle sales activities, and improve customer satisfaction.

This project is developed using Agile Methodology, which supports continuous improvement, flexibility, and incremental delivery of features to meet changing business requirements.

2. Problem Statement

Many organizations manage customer data manually or using disconnected systems such as spreadsheets. This leads to data inconsistency, poor customer follow-up, loss of potential leads, and inefficient communication. There is a need for a centralized and automated CRM system to manage customer relationships efficiently and securely.

3. Objectives of the Project

To centralize customer data management
To improve customer interaction and follow-up
To automate sales and lead tracking
To reduce manual work and data duplication
To enhance customer satisfaction and retention

4. Scope of the Project

The CRM system supports customer registration, lead management, contact tracking, sales status monitoring, and customer interaction history. Administrators can manage users, view reports, and analyze customer data to support business decisions.

5. Agile Methodology

Agile methodology emphasizes iterative development, customer feedback, and adaptability. The CRM system is developed in multiple sprints, with each sprint delivering a functional module of the system.

Agile Practices Followed

Incremental feature development
Continuous integration and testing
Regular feedback from stakeholders
Flexible and adaptive planning

6. Agile Development Process

Sprint 1
Requirement gathering
User authentication and role management

Sprint 2
Customer registration module
Customer profile management

Sprint 3
Lead management
Sales tracking module

Sprint 4
Reports and analytics
System testing and optimization

7. Functional Requirements

User login and authentication
Customer data management
Lead creation and tracking
Sales status monitoring
Customer interaction history

8. Non-Functional Requirements

